{{#css:
:root{
  --etest-accent:#ff1a5e;
}
.etest-hero{
  position:relative;
  border:1px solid #3a3440;
  background:linear-gradient(180deg,#1c1a1d,#232022);
  padding:24px;
  color:#f2e9ee;
  font-family:Georgia,serif;
}
.etest-corner{
  position:absolute; top:8px; left:8px; width:18px; height:18px;
  border:2px solid var(--etest-accent);
  border-right:none; border-bottom:none;
}
.etest-fixedcheck{
  position:fixed;
  bottom:10px; right:10px;
  background:#000; color:#fff; padding:4px 8px;
}
.etest-clipcheck{
  clip-path: circle(40% at 50% 50%);
  width:80px; height:80px; background:#ff1a5e;
}
.etest-blurcheck{
  backdrop-filter: blur(4px);
  -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(4px);
  width:80px; height:80px; background:rgba(255,255,255,0.2);
}
.etest-tab{
  font-family:monospace; font-size:12px; text-transform:uppercase;
  background:#1c1a1d; color:#9c8a96; border:1px solid #3a3440; padding:8px 12px; cursor:pointer;
}
.etest-tab:hover{ color:#fff; }
}}

== Test 1: {{#css:}} extension present + custom properties (var) ==
<div class="etest-hero">
  <span class="etest-corner"></span>
  If this box has a dark gradient background, a pink top-left corner bracket, and this text is off-white, the CSS extension AND CSS custom properties (var()) both work.
</div>

== Test 2: position:fixed (known TowersMUX rejection trigger) ==
<div class="etest-fixedcheck">FIXED BOX (should be pinned bottom-right if allowed)</div>
If Test 1's box above rendered UNSTYLED (plain HTML, no dark background), that means this whole {{#css:}} block was rejected wholesale because of this fixed-position rule.

== Test 3: clip-path ==
<div class="etest-clipcheck"></div>
Should be a pink circle if clip-path is allowed.

== Test 4: backdrop-filter ==
<div class="etest-blurcheck"></div>
Should be a translucent blurred box if backdrop-filter is allowed.

== Test 5: hover pseudo-class in extension CSS ==
<span class="etest-tab">HOVER ME</span>

== Test 6: raw script tag (expect stripped/escaped) ==
<script>document.write("SCRIPT EXECUTED");</script>
If you see literal "SCRIPT EXECUTED" text or the tag echoed as text below, that tells us how it's handled; if nothing appears, it was silently stripped.

== Test 7: canvas element (expect stripped) ==
<canvas id="etestCanvas" width="100" height="100" style="border:1px solid red;"></canvas>
If no red-bordered box appears above, canvas is stripped.

== Test 8: raw anchor tag and wikitext internal link (expect raw a stripped) ==
<a href="#nowhere">RAW A TAG</a>
[[Project:Sandbox|WIKITEXT INTERNAL LINK — should work]]

== Test 9: raw style tag (alternative to {{#css:}}) ==
<style>.etest-rawstyle{color:red;font-weight:bold;}</style>
<span class="etest-rawstyle">If this text is bold red, raw &lt;style&gt; tags work (not just the extension).</span>

